# What Vercel is asked to upload. The deployment there is the *browser* half of
# the game: the page, its JS, models, sounds and the /shared JSON. The Python
# game server cannot run on Vercel (its functions are request/response -- no
# WebSocket, no 30 Hz game loop, no shared memory between requests), so that half
# is deployed elsewhere; see README「部署」 for the two supported topologies.

# The server itself, and the tooling around it.
server/
tools/
Dockerfile
Procfile
render.yaml
requirements.txt
启动服务器.bat

# Source material that only the local dev tools use (Mixamo FBX originals and the
# old standalone demo). public/motions/ -- what the game actually loads -- ships.
new motion/
FPS father demo/
.trae/

